AI Gateway — Day 1

What is an AI Gateway?

An AI Gateway is a central layer between an application and AI/LLM providers.

   text
Application
     ↓
AI Gateway
     ↓
OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini


Why do we need it?

Without a gateway:

text Application → OpenAI
text Application → Anthropic


With a gateway:

  text
Application
     ↓
AI Gateway
     ↓
OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini


The gateway gives one central place to manage AI requests.

What can an AI Gateway do?

Routing — choose the right model/provider.
Authentication — check who is making the request.
Authorization — check what they are allowed to use.
Rate limiting — control the number of requests.
Caching — return an existing response without calling the model again.
Retry — try the same provider again when a temporary error happens.
Fallback — use another provider/model when the main one fails.
Security — protect sensitive data and apply policies.
Logging — record request details.
Cost tracking — track token usage and AI cost.

Important difference

Provider ≠ Model ≠ Gateway

   text
Application
     ↓
AI Gateway
     ↓
Provider
     ↓
Model


Application → sends the user's request.
AI Gateway → controls and manages the AI request.
Provider → provides access to AI models.
Model → generates the actual AI response.

 Main idea

AI Gateway is a centralized control layer for AI traffic.

It is more than just a proxy because it can handle routing, security, reliability, caching, monitoring, and cost control.
